# UrbanLuxe Portal — stack and workflow

This is **UrbanLuxe Portal**, a CRM/ERP for Dubai real estate. Owner: Asad (software engineer). Work in code directly; iterate by implementing, debugging, and shipping.

## Source of truth

- **GitHub repo:** https://github.com/asadknow-hub/urbanluxeportal.git
- **Default branch:** `main` — all work happens on `main` unless Asad explicitly asks for a different branch
- **Backend / DB / Auth / Storage:** Supabase (Postgres, Auth, Storage). Schema and changes live in `supabase/migrations/`. Prefer `supabase db push` / new numbered migrations over ad-hoc dashboard-only schema.
- **Hosting:** Vercel. Production is deployed from GitHub (`main`). Cron: `/api/cron/daily` in `vercel.json`.
- **App:** Next.js App Router (TypeScript). Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using Next APIs. UI: Tailwind + shadcn/ui.

## How to change things

- Prefer changes that stay compatible with **Supabase + Vercel**: env vars in `.env.local` locally and Vercel project settings in production. Never commit `.env*` or secrets.
- Database/API changes: migrations + typed clients in `src/lib/supabase/` and `src/types/database.ts`.
- Do not assume a separate custom backend. Server logic is Next.js route handlers / server actions talking to Supabase.
- After UI/UX work, follow `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md` (stack: Next.js + shadcn/ui).
- Do not push, force-push, or open PRs unless Asad asks. Do not commit unless asked.
